  "segment": "bootstrap-config",
  "source_text": "Arbiter uses Hydra as its configuration framework. Hydra composes Arbiter's runtime configuration from YAML files in the `conf` directory, then validates it against schemas provided by Arbiter and its plugins. Arbiter provides bootstrap commands that create initial configuration files you can edit to match your needs. First, create the server configuration. Then bootstrap the IMAP and SMTP account and policy templates. These files are starting points. Edit them to match your accounts, folders, and policy boundaries.",
